        "original_id": "399df8de-527f-5256-81a1-088966651fae",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Anatole Litvak, Kinji Fukasaku, Olivia de Havilland, Mark Stevens, Leo Genn, Celeste Holm, Beulah Bondi, Lee Patrick, Bunta Sugawara, Noboru Ando\n- Films: The Snake Pit, Street Mobster\n- Roles: filmmaker, director, producer, screenwriter\n- Topics: American drama films, Japanese yakuza films\n\nFacts:\n- Anatole Litvak was born on May 21, 1902, and he was a Russian-born American filmmaker who wrote, directed, and produced films in various countries and languages.\n- Kinji Fukasaku was born on July 3, 1930, and he was a Japanese film director and screenwriter.\n- The Snake Pit is a 1948 American drama film directed by Anatole Litvak and starring Olivia de Havilland, Mark Stevens, Leo Genn, Celeste Holm, Beulah Bondi, and Lee Patrick.\n- Street Mobster, known in Japan as Gendai Yakuza: Hitokiri Yota, is a 1972 Japanese yakuza film directed by Kinji Fukasaku and starring Bunta Sugawara and Noboru Ando.\n- Anatole Litvak died on December 15, 1974.\n- Kinji Fukasaku died on January 12, 2003.",
